  {
    "titulo": "Discussions Held with Air Liquide of France",
    "descricao": "On April 1, 2026, Mr. SAITO Tamotsu, Chairman of NEDO, and Mr. YOKOSHIMA Naohiko, President of NEDO, met with Mr. François Jackow, CEO of Air Liquide, France, and other members of the company’s executive management team. During the meeting, the participants exchanged views on the current status of hydrogen use and the challenges it faces in France, Europe as a whole, and Japan. They confirmed a shared desire to continue cooperating in the field of hydrogen. NEDO reaffirmed its commitment to comprehensive efforts toward the realization of a hydrogen-based society in Japan through R&D and demonstration projects. Overview of the meeting between NEDO and Air Liquide Commemorative photo of Mr. SAITO Tamotsu, Chairman of NEDO (right) and Mr. François Jackow, CEO of Air Liquide (left) Group photo of representatives from NEDO and Air Liquide (Center right: Mr. SAITO Tamotsu, Chairman of NEDO; far right: Mr. YOKOSHIMA Naohiko, President of NEDO; second from the left: Mr. MATSUMOTO Shintaro, Executive Director of NEDO; center left: Mr. François Jackow, CEO of Air Liquide; fourth from the left: Mr. Koji Makihara, President and CEO of Air Liquide Japan G.K.)",
